# Slack #coding-agents (Cursor main agent)

Channel: **`#coding-agents`** (`C0A9L7AU5HS`)
https://sumegroup.slack.com/archives/C0A9L7AU5HS

Same Jobs as the **status board** (`status-board.mdc`). Slack is the
**team-visible log**. Chase’s SoT for “what happened this turn” is the
**chat work report** (`end-of-turn-worker-brief.mdc`). Posting Slack
does **not** let you shrink or skip that report.

Chat/canvas do **not** show `확인됨`; Slack still marks resolve with a
check — **only on an allowed Slack window** (below).

Do not invent a second job list.

## Cadence (Chase lock 2026-09-08)

Slack MCP is **expensive**. It must **not** run every main-agent turn.

**Default: skip Slack this turn.** Chat + canvas still update.

Call Slack MCP only when **at least one** is true:

1. **4–5 user turns** since the last Slack write in this chat, **or**
2. **~30 minutes** since the last Slack write (desk or that Job), **or**
3. Chase **explicitly** asked to post / update Slack

When a window opens, do **one burst**: missing parents, at most one
digest reply per live Job thread, then lane reactions. Do not fire
Slack once per Job per turn.

**Forbidden every turn:** Slack search, parent post, replies,
`loading` / `eyes` / `white_check_mark`, `closed:` — just because
the board or a worker moved.

New Job / resolve / steer still wait for the same window unless
Chase asked for Slack now.

## When a Job is born (window only)

If there is no parent thread for that Job yet, **post a new channel
message** (not a reply). That message is the thread root.

Parent text (keep Job = terminal title):

```
<short Korean what> — `Opus : <slug> (#N)`
```

or Grok / Explore the same way. Slack MCP as the signed-in Chase user
(same pattern as historical “다음을 사용하여 보냄 @Cursor” posts).

Then set the parent reaction to **`loading`**.

Do **not** open a thread for a Job that already has a live parent.

## Updates (window only)

At most **one reply** per Job thread per burst. Do not edit the
parent into a changelog. Prefixes (existing desk voice):

| Prefix | When |
|--------|------|
| `working —` | doing the work |
| `5m —` | periodic snapshot (CI / MQ / leftover) |
| `steer —` | direction change |
| `HANDOFF —` | SHA / PR / leftover for the next owner |
| `closed:` | Chase stop / train ended |

No poll loop just to write `5m —`. The 5m prefix is **not** a 5-minute
Slack timer.

## Reactions = board lane (on the **parent**, window only)

| Board | Slack emoji (no colons) | When |
|-------|-------------------------|------|
| `지금` | `loading` | process still running |
| `스테이징` | `eyes` | finished, waiting Chase confirm |
| resolve | `white_check_mark` | Chase confirmed |

Move the lane reaction when the board lane moves **and** a Slack
window is open. Drop `loading` when leaving `지금`. `eyes` while in
스테이징/백로그. `white_check_mark` only on resolve (Job then drops
from chat/canvas immediately; Slack check can wait for the window).

## Non-goals

- Not a substitute for the **chat work report** or the chat status board
- Do not tell Chase to read Slack to understand the turn
- Do not dump secrets / PEM / tokens
- Codex / Claude Code as main: ignore (Cursor-only)
